expansion coefficients.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"APS"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"The 4D 4-point scattering amplitude of massless scalars via a massive exchange is expressed in a basis of conformal primary particle wavefunctions. This celestial amplitude is expanded in a basis of 2D conformal partial waves on the unitary principal series, and then rewritten as a sum over 2D conformal blocks via contour deformation. The conformal blocks include intermediate exchanges of spinning light-ray states, as well as scalar states with positive integer conformal weights. The conformal block prefactors are found as expected to be quadratic in the celestial OPE coefficients.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"control_number":1861169,"dois":[{"material":"publication","source":"APS","value":"10.1103/PhysRevD.104.126033"},{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1103/PhysRevD.104.126033"}],"preprint_date":"2021-04-27","arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["hep-th"],"value":"2104.13432"}],"titles":[{"source":"APS","title":"Conformal block expansion in celestial CFT"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Conformal Block Expansion in Celestial CFT"}],"document_type":["article"]}}],"total":1},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2104.13432&size=5&page=1&fields=titles,authors,dois,publication_info,arxiv_eprints,document_type,preprint_date,imprints,abstracts,urls","bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2104.13432&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2104.13432&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2104.13432&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2104.13432&size=5&page=1&fields=titles,authors,dois,publication_info,arxiv_eprints,document_type,preprint_date,imprints,abstracts,urls&format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2104.1